== Somen ==

Bring a #large pot{} of @water to a boil. You do not need to add salt. Simply add @somen noodles{4%bundles}(dried, wrapping removed). Spread the noodles around the pot in a circular motion to separate each strand, like opening a Japanese folding fan. Cook for ~{1%minute}, stirring occasionally with chopsticks, or generally according to package instructions.

> If it looks like the water may boil over, add a small amount of cold water to the pot. 

When the noodles are done, drain them in a #colander.

Rinse the somen under cold running water. Once the noodles are cool enough to handle, rinse them with your hands as if you are washing your clothes. Knead and massage the noodles to get rid of the excess oil. When you finish, transfer the somen to a #large bowl{} of @water{}(cold) with @ice cubes{}.

== Tsuyu (Dipping Sauce) ==

Depending on what you bought, the prep here varies. Straight Mentsuyu does NOT get diluted. 2 x Concentrated DOES get diluted with water. Be careful when purchasing, because Somen Tsuyu is for somen noodles, but Zaru / Soba Tsuyu is for soba. Generally, follow the instructions on the back, and add the sauce to a plate with an ice cube per person.

== Garnishing ==

Cut @?green onion{1}(thinly sliced) and grate @?ginger{1/2%inch} into small bowls. If you can find them, @?shiso leaves{} and @?myoga ginger{} are great for somen. Thinly slice and place them in separate small bowls. Grate a small amount of @?daikon radish{}, gently squeeze some of the liquid out, then place in a small bowl. Pour some @?toasted white sesame seeds{} into a small bowl. Gather all the garnishes on a tray, if desired, and set aside.
